id: pm-github-c093
title: "Preserve imported GitHub lifetimes, closure evidence and release attribution while linking cross-provider items"
description: "Repair the import root cause behind twelve Sourcery findings across six gated sync PRs. Preserve source timestamps through supported SDK metadata, map closure reasons and evidence, select tag-date release windows, report state conflicts, and link existing provider owners before creating items. Verify with recorded API fixtures and real temporary trackers at unchanged release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,fidelity,github,import
created_at: "2026-10-16T22:29:39.865Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T00:22:28.429Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T22:30:04.918Z",codex-agent,"Read all twelve unresolved Sourcery threads and the changed tracker/changelog files in the six consumer sync PRs. Scope: fix import only; preserve append-only history and leave unrelated closeout work untouched. The pinned SDK exposes completedAt but reserves created_at, updated_at and closed_at; source timestamp metadata plus an explicit SDK-gap receipt is required unless a supported import path proves otherwise. No upstream SDK issue will be filed under the queue rules."
  "2026-10-16T22:35:10.689Z",codex-agent,"Found public SDK import primitives beyond high-level create/update: item locks, canonical document serialization, before/after history entries and appendHistoryEntry. Implementing an idempotent finalization event with real native dates and source metadata, without modifying any historical record. Existing provider owners receive provenance links only; their content, native lifecycle, release and export identity remain authoritative. Local Git calendar tag dates select the first release at or after source closure; later closures remain pending. GraphQL ClosedEvent closer provides actual closing PR attribution where REST commit_id is null."
  "2026-10-16T23:09:24.995Z",codex-agent,"SDK candidate: bulk compensation captures native updated_at and passes it to restore as a history timestamp. Backdating that field disconnects the rollback version from its event. Preserve source creation/closure/completion natively for momentum and cycle time, and retain the exact source update date in github_updated_at while native updated_at stays the SDK mutation clock. Lifecycle finalization now runs at the SDK committing transition before the journal commits, with real compensation acceptance and a post-recovery idempotent check. No historical entries are rewritten."
  "2026-10-16T23:31:39.064Z",codex-agent,"Verified the SDK candidate with a real temporary tracker and public commitImportedItem/commitItemMutations calls: a historical native updated_at followed by an update and deliberate committing failure produces AggregateError, compensation_failed=true, original_restored=false. The importer retains the exact source update timestamp in github_updated_at while keeping native updated_at aligned with immutable event time. Real importer rollback acceptance restores the existing source lifecycle and deletes the newly created item. Focused corrections passed 7/7; final linked tests and unchanged full release gates are running."
  "2026-10-17T00:07:53.005Z",codex-agent,"The source-date, provider-link, privacy-plan and invalid-lifetime targeted checks pass 9/9 after certified SDK corpus reads replaced repeated CLI reads. A real tracker exposed the remaining canceled-to-completed transition: the SDK requires explicit repeat-closure authorization. Import reconciliation uses that supported transition with source closure evidence, and both modes now exercise canceled, completed and reopened states. The earlier release-gate probe had obsolete fixture assumptions and was stopped; final gates will run after these corrections."
  "2026-10-17T00:13:15.552Z",codex-agent,"Terminal reconciliation checks pass 3/3: canceled source records become completed when GitHub does, and reopen clears terminal evidence, in both import modes. Expanded provider matching also follows generic url/external_links when a provider id or tag declares ownership. Final release gates are being restarted against this complete implementation; no coverage thresholds, exemptions or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-17T00:22:28.429Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof at implementation 5999329: scratch copies retained the real recorded-API and temporary-tracker tests, rebuilding before each independent function control. Omitting persistImportFidelity yields 9 expected failures across source lifetime fixtures and state-conflict scenarios. Restoring generic importCloseReason wording yields 2 expected failures (beads and slack-standup); dropping linked closure evidence yields 1 (brief closing PR). Tag-only matchImportedIssue yields 2 expected failures (plain and atomic provider owner linking). Clearing buildImportFidelity release attribution yields 1 expected failure in the two-tag before/between/after fixture. Total: 15 expected behavioral failures, zero passes, skips or cancellations; no SDK mocks. Positive targeted checks passed 9/9, terminal transitions 3/3 and expanded identity checks 2/2. Full unchanged release gates remain in progress."
